<section id="coverage" class="route-band"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Supported scope</div><h2>Know what your history includes.</h2><p class="section-copy">Coverage depends on your plan, Shopify permissions, enabled observations, and retained evidence. Tracking starts after the relevant setup; it cannot recreate an earlier history Shopify did not provide.</p></div><div class="coverage-table" role="region" aria-label="StoreChronicle coverage" tabindex="0"><table><caption>Current feature coverage by plan</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Store data</th><th scope="col">Plan</th><th scope="col">What to expect</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Products and prices</th><td>Free, Standard, Pro</td><td>Supported product and variant field changes with available before-and-after values.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Collections and inventory</th><td>Standard, Pro</td><td>Supported collection fields, membership observations, and inventory quantities. Inventory requires additional access.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Orders</th><td>Pro</td><td>A limited order summary, not the full order or customer profile. Requires access and privacy setup.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Pages and themes</th><td>Pro</td><td>Configured observations of supported page and theme content. Observations do not capture every intervening edit.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Review rules and notifications</th><td>Standard, Pro</td><td>Rules flag matching changes for review. Optional email, Slack, Discord, and weekly summaries require setup and opt-in.</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">CSV export and read-only API</th><td>Pro</td><td>Export retained history or read it through the authenticated API, subject to the app’s limits.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p class="pricing-source">Restoration is selective and evidence-dependent: supported product, variant, collection, page, or inventory fields may be eligible. Order and theme restoration are not offered. StoreChronicle is not a whole-store backup.</p></div></section>
<section id="retention"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Two different retention periods</div><h2>Change history is not the same as restoration evidence.</h2><p class="section-copy">Shorter store settings and privacy deletion still apply. Evidence can expire while an ordinary change-history entry remains.</p></div><div class="feature-grid"><article class="card"><h3>Free</h3><p>$0 — no subscription charge.</p><p>Ordinary history: 7 days.</p><p>Activity and restoration evidence: up to 7 days.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Standard</h3><p>$9/month or $90/year.</p><p>Ordinary history: 90 days.</p><p>Activity and restoration evidence: up to 90 days.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Pro</h3><p>$19/month or $190/year.</p><p>Ordinary history: no automatic age-based expiry while installed.</p><p>Activity and restoration evidence: up to 120 days, with either billing interval.</p></article></div><p class="pricing-source">Choose monthly or annual billing for either paid plan. Annual billing costs the equivalent of ten monthly payments, saving about 17%. Both intervals include the same features and retention within each plan. No usage-based overages. After a confirmed downgrade, a seven-day read-only ordinary-history export grace helps you preserve accessible history. It does not extend restoration, activity evidence, or other higher-plan features. Uninstall and privacy deletion take precedence.</p></div></section>
<section id="faq" class="route-band"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><div class="section-kicker">Common questions</div><h2>Before you use StoreChronicle.</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Does StoreChronicle identify exactly who made a change?</summary><p>No. It can show optional Shopify-reported activity labels where available. These labels are not verified staff identities, and related activity is not proof of who caused a specific recorded change. Unknown attribution stays unknown.</p></details><details><summary>Can I roll back my entire Shopify store?</summary><p>No. StoreChronicle is not a whole-store backup or disaster-recovery service. Selective restoration is limited to eligible retained fields, requires Shopify permissions and confirmation, and cannot reverse every downstream effect. Other apps or staff can make concurrent edits.</p></details><details><summary>Does it record every change in real time?</summary><p>No. Supported Shopify events and configured observations provide evidence, but delayed delivery, outages, access restrictions, and observation intervals can leave gaps. The app shows recovery and unresolved-gap information instead of claiming missing history is complete.</p></details><details><summary>Can I export my history?</summary><p>Pro includes formula-safe CSV export and a read-only API. Exports cover available, entitled records; multi-part exports are not an atomic snapshot of the entire store. A confirmed downgrade also provides a seven-day read-only ordinary-history export grace.</p></details><details><summary>What happens when I uninstall?</summary><p>Authenticated Shopify uninstall and shop-deletion notifications trigger store-data cleanup. Reinstalling does not guarantee recovery of deleted history. Backup copies and external recipients have separate handling, explained in the <a href="/privacy.html#storechronicle">StoreChronicle privacy disclosure</a>.</p></details><details><summary>Is StoreChronicle available on the Shopify App Store?</summary><p>Not yet. The app is in development-store validation and its App Store listing is being prepared. Contact <a href="mailto:support@attahirlabs.com">support@attahirlabs.com</a> with questions. This page does not represent Shopify approval.</p></details></div></div></section>
